It owns explicit state\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:732:identity, that parked it. This is a decided rule for B4 and R4, not a\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:772:the B6 linker. This rule is deliberate; the alternative was a pair\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:778:R2 defines the data contract R4 will interpret. It does not execute an\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:780:`yin.vm.debruijn-register-effects`; R4 must reuse them rather than invent\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:790:`runtime` is an explicit map containing the validated image, R, pc,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:845:    {:segment <validated register image>\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:866:    {:segment <validated register image>\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:877:which register layout owns a frame. R4 may share persistent image values in\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:913:validated register payload and the documented FFI keys.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:918:and may not be read because the image was liveness-validated. For\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:955:reader keys. `ffi/response-wait-entry` must satisfy this rule before R4\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:960:R4 uses `engine/scheduler-round` and the three-argument restore directly.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1058:10. R2 tests do not instantiate a register VM. R4 must later prove that its\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1072:Informational only, and sequenced after R4: it runs identical pure-program\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1073:corpora through the stack VM and the real R4 kernel, never a stand-in\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1080:### R4: register kernel\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1088:a validated register image and its R. R4 follows B3's own precedent and\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1101:before R2 lands; R4 is complete only when both tiers are.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1104:track, R2's descriptor and liveness extension and R4's pure-program tier,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1105:then R4's effects tier once B4 and R2 exist, then R3 against the real\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1108:before R2 or R4.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1154:1. R0-R2 are lowerer and format work. R4, the register kernel, is\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1188:    shapes, and validation as pure data before R4 interprets them. The\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1196:  pairing's trust rests on; R4 and B6 are both decided phases.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1200:The lowerer-only end condition is a validated, deterministic register image\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1204:with both R4 tiers complete, the R3 report published for the owner to read,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1215:image contract and the landed R4 register kernel.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1225:> `01a14f30-ca56-7530-bb93-3a870eca7a7b`; reviewer thread:\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1364:Same-layout native payloads with admissible values round-trip between reference\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1375:reconstruct self-consistent segment/hash/live metadata, and apply normal native\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1378:gate the native transport API to a verified matching layout/prefix or return\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1400:`[[empty-R 0 0]]` offset-table rules, and the 65,536-slot preallocated function\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1415:lowering validates binding/format, attached origin, and arity against actual\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1424:**W0 and Rust K0 are the same conformance-kit deliverable**, exported from R4,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1436:- the format-level trace R4 produces (sparse continuation payload at every boundary, `K` depth, saved register pairs).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1445:- a wide-body fixture whose register count exceeds `65,535`,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1492:the wide-register (`>65,535`) and million-tail cases.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1506:recursion and long tail recursion. Assert guest `K` behavior and bounded native\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1516:native↔CLJS admissible payload round-trips and identical qualified refusals.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1517:Implement native payload/owner/type validation before this gate.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1529:restoration, snapshot alias isolation, and both native\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1532:same-process tests. Assert native `continuation-defect` recomputes the same\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1604:validates arity/format and private store behavior. GC tests retain captured\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1642:binary artifacts validate. Run focused JVM reference tests with the existing\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1646:harness in that lane. Add dedicated native Wasmtime and Wasmer harness tasks\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1648:native runtimes against the reference. No native lane may be reduced to\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1651:no duplicate effects and no JS/WASI dependencies in native execution. Register\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1661:native stack depth, arena/heap retention, call/suspension, stream bytes/copy/codec\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1666:not a service-migration or alternative architecture experiment. K3 may measure\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1668:not evidence it is faster.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1672:opcode/contract version, no alternate A→R register allocator, no native stack\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1674:beyond the established native register fragment.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1681:- **K2:** payload/effect descriptor canonical bytes equal R4, including every return frame's `:live`; bidirectional Rust↔R4 restore and equal `continuation-defect` refusal rules.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1683:- **K4:** deterministic translator bytes across runs/platforms, full-kit interpreted/native boundary and refusal equality, artifact-drop fallback, and interpretation with no toolchain plus `:unsupported`.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1684:- **K5:** shared engine parity and blocked-machine wire round-trips with JVM R4 in both directions.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1687:coverage advances alongside the W slices and cannot be omitted because native\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
